---
import * as icons from "@grave/animated-icons/astro";
import { commerceCurrencyIcons } from "../../../../helpers/commerce-currency";
const sizes = [14, 16, 24, 28];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head><meta charset="utf-8" /><title>Commerce and currency recipe comparisons</title></head>
  <body>
    <h1>Commerce and currency recipe comparisons</h1>
    <p>The reference executes all fifteen original Lucide Animated React components from revision 4662fff2b60fdcf4751b32013606756caf7c4c26. Their class utility import points to a local equivalent. React is confined to comparison pages.</p>
    <p>Hover a row or use its Replay button to animate both versions. Play all starts every sample. Stop all returns them to rest. Seek pauses the current playback at the selected time.</p>
    <p>All copied sources change only the class utility import. Cart keeps separate scale and repeated vertical timing. Its vertical transition uses the implicit easeOut curve and finishes its remaining pulses when normal returns the scale. Wallet keeps its explicit 12px 12px SVG origin. CreditCard transforms its inner group. The currency symbols preserve their original main and secondary paths, independent opacity durations, and delayed entry and return.</p>
    <p>Automated returns capture a seeked entry pose and reset velocity on both CreditCard versions before stopping. Native opacity poses are captured before replacement. Cart keeps its original y animation running, and seeks that track relative to the captured entry time. Manual Stop all uses the original upstream method. Adapter tests check interrupted continuity, replay, cleanup, and reduced motion. Interrupted spring velocity parity is not established by these measurements. Visual acceptance remains with manual review.</p>
    <button type="button" id="play">Play all</button>
    <button type="button" id="stop">Stop all</button>
    <label>Playback time in milliseconds <input id="time" type="number" value="200" min="0" max="5000" step="50" /></label>
    <button type="button" id="seek">Seek and pause</button>
    {commerceCurrencyIcons.map(icon => {
      const Component = icons[icon.name];
      return <section>
        <h2>{icon.name}</h2>
        <p><a href={`https://github.com/pqoqubbw/icons/blob/4662fff2b60fdcf4751b32013606756caf7c4c26/icons/${icon.slug}.tsx`}>Pinned upstream recipe</a> · <a href={`/${icon.slug}/`}>Manual controls and lifecycle</a></p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Astro adapter</th><th>Upstream React component</th><th>Playback</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{sizes.map(size => <tr data-icon={icon.slug} data-size={size}>
            <th scope="row">{size} px</th>
            <td data-adapter><Component size={size} controlled /></td>
            <td><div data-reference data-name={icon.name} data-size={size}></div></td>
            <td><button type="button" data-replay aria-label={`Replay ${icon.name} at ${size} pixels`}>Replay</button></td>
          </tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
      </section>;
    })}
  </body>
</html>

<script>
  import "../commerce-currency-reference";
</script>
